       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose this high risks serious hepatotoxicity.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is also double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nNormal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't change these limits.\n\nHere are some options that would fit the limits:\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you meant 2000 mg as the total daily dose, I can enter it in divided doses, for example 650 mg three times daily. If you really want the dose as written, please confirm that. Tell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
